<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa extends Thai code-sharing.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa extends Thai code-sharing.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG said it will extend its code-sharing agreement with Thai Airways International to new Asian destinations from October 27.</p>
<p>Lufthansa will add a third weekly Munich to Bangkok flight and offer four weekly services from Frankfurt to the Thai capital as code-share flights, a company statement said.</p>
<p>Daily direct flights to the Thai destinations of Chiang Rai, Hat Yai and Surat Thani and to Taipei will be flown by Thai Airways from Bangkok as joint code flights, a Lufthansa statement said.</p>
<p>A third code-share flight from Frankfurt via Bangkok to Auckland will also be started, it added.</p>
<p>--Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 8982 Fax +44 171 542 5017</p>
